@FG-M1-bbde8b1664 CORRECT conf=M cls=CLASSIFICATION
why: Stored CO on GOV-013, GOV-014, SEC-006 and SEC-008, HIGH. Those policies bind implementation, while this line binds what a scan recommends. A scan report that recommends blanket field encryption as optional hardening, with nothing implemented, satisfies every cited policy and breaks this line. The entailment test fails for the act of recommending. Prefer smallest secure change is also not stated in any policy. The canonical part is real for what the recommendation would ask to implement.
q: .claude/skills/security-scan/SKILL.md:201-205 | Prefer the smallest secure change consistent with project architecture.
q: .claude/skills/security-scan/SKILL.md:201-205 | blanket encryption of all database fields
